{
 "section_summary": "This section completes a July 1949 Japanese radio-station directory, listing frequencies, call signs, SCAP registration numbers, station locations, and an administrative key to prefecture codes. It then documents U.S. efforts to stop interference, traced to Hamhung in northern Korea, with an aircraft-control frequency used in Japan, including a State Department instruction and diplomatic correspondence with the Soviet government. The final pages transmit and reproduce a November 1949 amendment to the Japanese station list, recording additions, deletions, relocations, frequency changes, and revised call signs, including AFRS stations.",
